      {
        "id": 243837,
        "name": "Rabit",
        "username": "Rabit",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
        "created_at": "2022-03-24T17:50:00.856Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"JoeSteeloak\" data-post=\"24\" data-topic=\"29197\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/joesteeloak/48/4853_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> JoeSteeloak:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Christopher’s way of using tokens is the way we do it too and you never run out of them that way even if playing both Unity and Captain Cosmic.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>We discussed this while playing on Tuesday, and noted that we couldn’t read the HP of the cards from across the table, but with the tokens we could easily tell highest/lowest, etc. (Our usual group is 5 people, so it’s not a small table.) So we add tokens from the start. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/confused.png?v=12\" title=\":confused:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":confused:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
